#Opening Hand Probability
OPENING_HAND_PROBABILITY = $$\begin{equation*} P(X \ge k) = \sum_{x=k}^{\min(n, K)} \frac{\binom{K}{x} \binom{N-K}{n-x}}{\binom{N}{n}} \end{equation*}$$
# $N = 99$ (Deck size excluding Commander)
# $n = 7$ (Hand size)
# $K =$ Number of target cards in deck (e.g., 10 ramp spells)
# $x =$ Desired number in opening hand

